1
00:00:00,267 --> 00:00:02,733
Hard conversations rarely get a second
take.

2
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:05,059
DialogIQ lets you practice one.

3
00:00:06,633 --> 00:00:08,576
Say it badly. Rewind. Try again.

4
00:00:10,167 --> 00:00:12,711
Built by Pramodh and a team of AI agents.

5
00:00:13,067 --> 00:00:14,992
Powered by Meta's Muse Spark Open.

6
00:00:15,333 --> 00:00:16,386
Now meet Bob.

7
00:00:19,333 --> 00:00:22,619
Here's DialogIQ. Pick a conversation
you're dreading.

8
00:00:23,633 --> 00:00:27,418
Today: Bob. He missed his Q3 deadlines,
and he's on the defensive.

9
00:00:27,733 --> 00:00:31,424
You get his opening line, your situation,
and a coach on the side.

10
00:00:32,233 --> 00:00:33,542
First, lead with pressure.

11
00:00:37,833 --> 00:00:39,583
He explains, but stays guarded.

12
00:00:41,833 --> 00:00:43,565
The coach suggests a different move.

13
00:00:47,533 --> 00:00:48,469
So, rewind.

14
00:00:50,333 --> 00:00:53,209
Back to the moment before it went wrong.
Second take.

15
00:00:55,833 --> 00:00:58,758
Acknowledge it's been hard. Then ask
what's in the way.

16
00:01:02,133 --> 00:01:03,106
He opens up.

17
00:01:05,533 --> 00:01:06,810
Now, offer real help.

18
00:01:11,733 --> 00:01:13,137
And he names what he needs.

19
00:01:15,833 --> 00:01:18,712
Pressure: guarded. Empathy: open, two
needs uncovered.

20
00:01:20,933 --> 00:01:23,469
Bob runs on Muse Spark Open through
Baseten.

21
00:01:23,833 --> 00:01:27,903
Local rules track stance. A separate judge
counts needs uncovered.

22
00:01:28,300 --> 00:01:33,139
Fireworks hosts the coach. It sees the
conversation, never Bob's hidden needs.

23
00:01:34,733 --> 00:01:36,170
Do these hints fit the moment?

24
00:01:36,567 --> 00:01:42,892
In a small test graded by agents: 52
usable hints out of 78. Before, 23.

25
00:01:43,533 --> 00:01:47,430
In one stop-request case, all six hints
respected Bob's request.

26
00:01:49,067 --> 00:01:51,151
Same moment. Different first move.

27
00:01:51,567 --> 00:01:53,049
That is the power of practice.

28
00:01:54,500 --> 00:01:57,885
DialogIQ. Practice the conversation before
it matters.

29
00:01:58,233 --> 00:02:00,862
Find the project on GitHub. Link below.

